CyberArk Data Flow Diagram (DFD)
This document outlines the data flow architecture for CyberArk privileged access workflows, including individual admin access, team/shared safes, bot account management, and workforce password manager access.
1. Privileged Individual Admin Account Workflow
Step 1: User requests access via SailPoint IIQ (AD Role: ACU Admins)
Step 2: Upon approval, CyberArk provisions an Individual Safe (IND_SamAccountName_EmpID)
Step 3: Retrieve permissions assigned
Step 4: Admin account created (A_SamAccountName) and stored in safe
Step 5: User requests access to target application using admin account
2. Team / Shared Safe Workflow
Step 1: Team requests AD group (CARK_ACU_TeamName)
Step 2: Owners and members are added
Step 3: CyberArk creates Team Safe (APP_SVC_TeamName or shared format)
Step 4: Accounts are vaulted into safe for shared usage
3. Bot Account Onboarding and Management
Step 1: Team requests AD group (CARK_ACU_TeamName)
Step 2: CyberArk creates AAM_APP Safe
Step 3: Bot accounts onboarded
Step 4: Automated password rotation enabled
4. Workforce Password Manager (Access)
Step 1: User requests access via IIQ to App_CyberArkPWUser_Authentication_Prod
Step 2: Access granted via Okta tile
Step 3: User launches Access Portal to manage credentials
High-Level Data Flow Representation
IIQ -> Active Directory -> CyberArk Safes -> Accounts -> End Users/Application Access
IIQ -> Okta -> CyberArk Access Portal
